<title>THAILAND: THAI MONEY MARKET CLOSED FOR QUEEN'S BIRTHDAY.</title>
<headline>THAI MONEY MARKET CLOSED FOR QUEEN'S BIRTHDAY.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Thai money market and commercial banks closed on Tuesday to mark Queen Sirikit's birthday.</p>
<p>The baht was quoted offshore at 31.450/31.520 to the dollar on Tuesday morning against 31.150/31.200 late on Monday.</p>
<p>The baht held steady in the domestic market on Monday, unaffected by reports that the International Monetary Fund and other Asian donors pledged to provide a $16 billion loan package for Thailand.</p>
